# .worktreeinclude — gitignored local docs that every parallel worktree needs
# for full context. Synced by scripts/sync-worktree-docs.ps1 <worktree-path>
# after a worktree is created from origin/main.
#
# RULE: NEVER list secrets here (appsettings.Local.json, .env.local, *.pem,
# *.tfstate). Only the stack-owner main checkout runs against real secrets;
# the sync script refuses secret-like entries.
#
# Entries may be files, directories, or globs (resolved relative to repo root).

# Session-state source of truth (gitignored, ADR 0072 docs-privacy)
docs/current-work.md
docs/current-work-archive.md
docs/steg-tracker.md

# docs/tech-debt.md + docs/tech-debt-archive.md were REMOVED from this list
# 2026-08-02 (ADR 0121, PR #1173) when the TD register was retired.
#
# Not merely because they are obsolete — because keeping them was measured harmful.
# The reaper derives its rescue pathspec straight from this file and treats every
# entry as landable session state: main copy has it + worktree copy differs ->
# "UNLANDED EDIT: land it there, then reap". Measured on the day of the change:
# 11 of the 20 sibling worktrees carried a pre-retirement register (101–108 kB across
# four vintages) against the main copy's 3 435 B tombstone, so all eleven would have
# become permanently unreapable — the main copy is the 21st and is never reaped — and
# the remedy the hook prints ("land it there") is the one thing the retirement
# forbids, since it would overwrite the tombstone with an old register copy.
#
# Nothing is lost by not syncing them: CLAUDE.md §1.6 is TRACKED and read on every
# invocation, so a fresh worktree learns the register is retired from the file it
# already reads. The backlog is GitHub Issues; parked entries are in #1172.

# Per-session logs + local agent reviews + local ADRs for context.
# (The ADR globs mirror .gitignore's — the derivation lives there, in one place.
# The 01-glob was added 2026-07-10 with ADR 0100.)
docs/sessions/
docs/reviews/
docs/decisions/00[789][0-9]-*.md
docs/decisions/01[0-9][0-9]-*.md
# ADR 0005 is gitignored but matched by NEITHER glob above, so it reached no worktree at
# all. It is cited from PRODUCTION code — JobAdsEndpoints.cs and SavedSearchesEndpoints.cs
# for the auth-gating decision, Program.cs for the cost-protection amendment — as well as
# from tracked ADRs and the budget_actions Terraform module. Re-measure with
#   git ls-files -z | xargs -0 grep -l "ADR 0005"
# and read the result as a PROPERTY, not a count: files that merely describe this entry
# are not citations, and a name-based exclusion list cannot keep up now that .gitignore
# obliges more homes to name the ADR. That is the load-bearing shape the handoff-oversikt
# entry below names. Listed on that measurement (2026-08-17); keeping it out of worktrees
# instead is Klas's call to state.
docs/decisions/0005-*.md

# GDPR Art. 30 processing-register (ROPA) — local-only (ADR 0072 / #183), internal
# accountability record. Worktrees need it for GDPR context; never a secret.
docs/runbooks/gdpr-processing-register.md
# The v3 design spec ADR 0052 transcribes from and cites as authoritative (#1095/#1103).
# Gitignored (.gitignore:104) but load-bearing: without it a reviewer greps, finds nothing, and
# re-derives "drift" — which is exactly how #1095 was born.
docs/handoff-oversikt/
